(a) whether the share of manufacturing in Gross Value Added (GVA) of economy showed no improvement in the indicator ever since launch of Make in India campaign in 2014;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) details of steps taken to improve share of manufacturing in GVA of economy to bring it up from current 14.7 per cent of economy, the lowest since 1968-69, through Make in India initiative;
(d) whether there has been any improvement in share of manufacturing in GVA post-pandemic; and
(e) if so, the details of post-pandemic steps taken to attract more investment in economy to increase manufacturing share of GVA?

(a) whether Government has recently extended the validity of Coastal Regulation Zone (CRZ) clearances for ten years against the present provision of seven years;
(b) if so, reasons therefor;
(c) whether before notification, public opinion was not sought for objections and suggestions;
(d) if so, reasons therefor;
(e) whether Government has provisioned for the transfer of projects to any legal proponent and splitting of projects into two or more projects, details thereof;
(f) whether this amendment will spur tourism, which may impact the fragile ecosystem of CRZ, thereby deepening the climate crisis; and
(g) if so, the actions  which will be taken to mitigate this?

(a) the details of aftermath of the Silkyara accident, including injuries or fatalities so far; 
(b) whether the same part of the tunnel had earlier collapsed in 2019, if so, whether a feasibility report was prepared before beginning;
(c) whether there is a rule mandating provision of building escape routes in long tunnel projects to facilitate rescue work in case of any emergency;
(d) whether any Expert Committee has been constituted to investigate the causes of the accident, if so, the details thereof; and
(e) whether Government would abandon the project or re-evaluate in view of the weak rock base?

(a) whether Government aware of the Annual Status of Education Report 2023 findings that state that nearly 25 per cent of rural youth in the age group of 14 to 18 cannot read a class 2 level text “fluently” even if it is in their regional language; 
(b) if so, the details of the findings and the reasons therefor; and
(c) the details of the number of rural youth within this age group who can “fluently” read a class 2 level text in English and their regional language divided State-wise and initiatives designed to address this disparity?

(a) whether the monthly GST collections are increasing across the country;
(b) if so, the details of the last 12 months, State-wise and month-wise;
(c) whether this increase is due to inflation or any other factors are responsible for this hike;
(d) if so, the reasons therefor;
(e) whether Government envisions bringing petroleum products under the umbrella of GST; and
(f) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a)	whether there has been an increase in number of false advertisements by Ayush manufacturers after omission of Rule 170 from Drugs and Cosmetic Rules (2018) last year;
(b)	if so, the details thereof, including the number of complaints received about such misleading representations by the ASCI and GAMA portal during the last five years;
(c)	the details of ASCI standards on misleading claims regarding AYUSH products;
(d)	whether Government plans to tackle this menace and stick to standards issued by ASCI, including re-introduction of Rule 170;
(e)	if so, the details thereof including initiatives to tackle this and guidelines issued to States; and
(f)	if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government is aware that a large number of workers in the unorganized sector continue to work past the age of 60;
(b) if so, reasons regarding setting age limits between 16-59 to register on the e-Shram portal and the resultant consequences;
(c) details of the estimated number of workers above the age of 60 working in the unorganized sector and strategies for their inclusion; and
(d) details of strategies to fix the issues with e-Shram portal registration, including non-linkage of mobile number to Aadhaar, dormant nature of linked bank account, switching mobile numbers or multiple individuals using the same number?

K

(a) the details of the total number of registrations, State-wise, on the e-Shram portal since 2021 and the percentage of these recognised as unorganised sector labour;
(b) the details of the social security benefits provided to those who register on the portal and the total number of current pensioners along with pension contribution from Government after integration with PM-SYM;
(c) whether Government plans to bring about an employment guarantee scheme for urban labour modelled on MGNREGA Scheme;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) if not, the reasons therefor?

K

(a) the details of absolute number and percentage of total highway users/registered vehicles with FASTags in India currently;
(b) whether directions were issued to collect double toll as penalty in case of no FASTag or inoperable FASTag or deficient balance in account linked to FASTag;
(c) if so, details of the amount of toll collected since the penalty was imposed, including details of penalty amount & number of transactions and users who were penalised in the last 12 months; and
(d) whether Government intends to continue with this double toll collection and if so, the rationale of this penalty imposed?

K

(a) whether Government has plans to introduce a comprehensive definition of 'healthy foods' for the country so that companies do not have to resort to using their own definitions;
(b) if so, the details thereof, including possible guidelines, separate taxes on unhealthy foods especially those catered towards children, etc.; and
(c) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether it is a fact that the reports of over 10 crores of the 50 crores plus PM Jan Dhan Yojana (PMJDY) accounts are currently missing or untraceable;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) if so, whether this means that ?40,000 crores or more of this Scheme is locked up in banks without any use to poor beneficiaries;
(d) whether 14 per cent of the total number of PMJDY accounts continue to be inoperative as accepted by the Ministry in August 2021; and
(e) the details of the current number of inoperative accounts under the Scheme and whether the majority of them continue to be accounts of women?

K

(a) whether it is a fact that there has been a reduction of General and Sleeper Class tickets in place of AC tickets in trains across the country, if so, the details thereof;
(b) if not, the aggregate coach compositions of trains over the last five years, details of the share of sleeper berths compared to the AC berths;
(c) whether there has been any increase/decrease in people opting for non-AC tickets in the country; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether NCR is reeling under severe air pollution for the last two months;
(b) if so, details thereof along with responsible factors; 
(c) whether Government has devised any foolproof mechanism to ensure pollution-free and clean air to  capital's population;
(d) if so, details thereof, if not, reasons therefor;
(e) details of amount spent to combat air pollution in NCR during last three years, divided into categories of tools used;
(f) whether Government is contemplating using artificial rain to mitigate this menace; and
(g) if so, details thereof, including scientifically-proven positive and negative consequences of artificial rain on general population?

(a) whether India has deported 41 Canadian diplomats under the Vienna Convention on Diplomatic Relations of 1961;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Canadian Government has closed its consulate general offices in Mumbai, Bengaluru and Hyderabad which is affecting visa processing of Indian students who are scheduled to visit Canada for higher studies; and
(c) the remedial steps Government would put in place to ameliorate the problems of the student community as a consequence of the strained relations with Canada?

J

(a) whether recently there was a report regarding the leakage of CoWin data and Ministry of Health and Family Welfare termed this news as baseless and mischievous, yet proposed to get the inquiry done by CERN-IN;
(b) whether the Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology stated that there was no direct leakage of data and the present leakage news belongs to previous data hacking, thereby accepting the leakage, if so, the reasons for conflicting reports by two entities of Government;
(c) whether Delhi police has made some arrests from Bihar, in connection with hacking of data; and
(d) the measures Government will take to protect the privacy of citizens data?

(a) whether the Narcotics Control Bureau (NCB) is aware of the large scale trafficking of drugs in Manipur;
(b) the details of such drugs seized in the State and those sourcing from the State;
(c) whether there is a nexus among narcotics business and terrorist activities in the State and it is one of the factors fueling the present state of affairs, the details thereof; and
(d) the actions taken and contemplated to be done thereon?

arv

(a) the total number of farmers in the country and how many of them are getting PM-Kisan Samman Nidhi;
(b) whether ?6,000 provided under the scheme is sufficient to meet the requirments of farmers;
(c) whether some States are also proposing to supplement the funds provided under the scheme by Central Government to the farmers, if so, the details of the States and the amount committed; and
(d) whether Government plans to increase the annual amount, or even to credit the entire annual amount in one instalment, instead of the three instalments, as paid currently, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has launched the Production Linked Incentive (PLI) Scheme for many sectors including medical devices, bulk drugs, white goods, telecom etc.;
(b) the total outlay and expenditure on PLI scheme since its inception and the estimated additional capital investment generated from the PLI scheme;
(c) whether any assessments have been made on the new employment opportunities thus created, if so, the details thereof, sector-wise; and
(d) whether Government is extending PLI schemes in sectors like toys and leather and if so, the criteria and procedure for selection of an industry or sector for inclusion in PLI scheme?

(a) whether Government authorities had shut down the services of Twitter and raid homes of executives of Twitter for their coverage of farmers' agitation during 2021, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the number of requests made by Government from August 2020 to December 2021 to Twitter to remove such content and the number of requests for user account data; and
(c) whether these requests were complied with along with the number of requests accepted or rejected by Twitter?

(a) the status of existing vacancies in the various posts under the various departments of Railways;
(b) the details of the total number of existing apprentices and the number of apprentices who received permanent posts after the apprenticeship program over the last five years, year-wise; and
(c) whether Railways is proposing to restart the Special Class Railway Apprenticeship program as recommended by the Ministry of Finance?

(a)	the total number of deaths of cattle due to the outbreak of Lumpy Skin Disease (LSD), State-wise; 
(b)	whether Government has provided compensation to all the farmers who lost cattle due to the disease; 
(c)	if so, the details thereof, State-wise; 
(d)	if not, the reasons therefor;
(e)	whether ICAR has developed a vaccine for cow, buffalo specifically, and what trials have been conducted in this regard; and
(f)	if so, whether the vaccine developed by ICAR has been approved and included in the vaccination program?

arv

(a) whether Government has conducted an assessment study of the Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana(PMKVY) on the employability of the workforce;
(b) the number of training centres that were closed during the pandemic and its impact on the skill development program, State-wise;
(c) the status of the first batch of Indian Skill Development Service(ISDS) inducted by Government in 2019; and
(d) whether Government is proposing to start recruitment on yearly basis to ISDS and if so, the details thereof?

D

(a) whether Government is aware that several people died while cleaning sewers and septic tanks in the country in the last five years;
(b) if so, the details thereof, State-wise;
(c) the current status of the ban on Manual Scavenging and number of cases that have been registered for persons employing Manual Scavengers, State-wise;
(d) the steps taken by Government to ensure a complete ban on manual scavenging; and
(e) whether Government has taken any other initiative to replace Manual Scavenging, and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of cases registered under the Prevention of Money Laundering Act against former or sitting Members of Parliament, Members of State Legislative Assemblies, and Members of Legislative Councils in the last five years, year-wise;
(b) the details of the number of cases pending against sitting or Ex MPs and MLAs in the last five years, year-wise; and
(c) the number of cases registered under the Prevention of Money Laundering Act that resulted in a conviction in the last five years, year-wise?

(a)	the details of the amount collected under District Mineral Fund, year-wise and State-wise, since 2017;
(b)	whether the amount collected under District Mineral Fund is utilized as per the mandate of the Mines and Minerals (Development and Regulation) Amendment Act, 2015;
(c)	whether the cases of delays in the utilization of funds have been found by Government; and 
(d)	whether Government has issued any timeline for the funds to be utilized, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of the agencies that are the funding source for the NCRTC projects and the details on total available funds with NCRTC for financing RRTS projects;
(b) the details of the total cost of the Delhi-Meerut RRTS project and the amount of funds available for the implementation of this project;
(c) the details of the total amount of money utilized for the Delhi-Meerut RRTS project till date; and
(d) the details of the trial of the 17-km priority section of the Delhi-Meerut RRTS project in Ghaziabad?

(a) whether Government is aware of the increased instances of hate-mongering in news debates on TV news channels;
(b) whether Government is considering codifying the existing Code of Ethics and Broadcasting Standards; and 
(c) whether Government proposes to enact a law prohibiting hate speech in the country?

(a)	the number of cases of human trafficking in women, men, and children in the last five years, year-wise and State-wise/UT-wise details thereof;
(b)	the number of trafficked survivors who got rehabilitated by Government in the last five years, year-wise and State-wise/UT-wise details thereof;
(c)	the preventive steps taken by Government to stop human trafficking cases; and
(d)	the status of the Anti-trafficking bill and the reasons for its delay in introducing it in the Parliament?

(a) the list of the total number of waste-to-energy plants in the country as on November 2022 including the details of the number of plants that are shut down, State-wise;
(b) the reasons for the failure of plants and the estimated loss to Government because of shutting down plants;
(c) the waste to the energy potential and the average cost per unit generation of power from the plant; and
(d) the details of the number of plants against which there are pending court cases for non-compliance of pollution norms?

(a) the total number of cesses that are being levied by Government and the amount collected through each cess separately in the last five years, year-wise;
(b) whether the total amount collected through cesses was fully utilized for the specific purpose for which the cess was collected in the last five years;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and 
(d) if not, the reasons for its underutilization?

(a) the State-wise details on the number of cities which still do not have a Town Vending Committee as per the mandate of the Street Vendors (Protection of Livelihood and Regulation of Street Vending) Act, 2014;
(b) the steps taken by Government to ensure that Town Vending Committee is established in every State;
(c) whether Government is aware that the ceiling of 2.5 percent of the population of the city, town, zone, and ward on street vendors is inadequate; and
(d) if so, whether Government is planning to increase the ceiling or to rehabilitate the workers associated with street vending to some other work?

(a)	the details of the number of foreign companies that participated in the auction of coal mines since the first auction in the year 2020 and the companies that won the bid and currently working in this sector;
(b)	the details of investments made under Foreign Direct Investment in the sector, year-wise and State-wise;
(c)	the steps taken by Government to attract foreign investments in the sector; and
(d)	whether all the operating coal mines have valid environmental clearances, if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the amount collected through Agriculture Infrastructure Development Cess introduced in the Union Budget 2021-22;
(b) the utilization of the Agriculture Infrastructure Development Cess on creating Agriculture Infrastructure Fund; and
(c) the details of disbursement of Agriculture Infrastructure Fund for the agriculture sector since its introduction in May 2020?
